A. Each of Fisher's groups on its own: chi-squared per degree of freedom, and the chance of so small a value if honest
   seven            2.1389 on  7: 0.306 a degree; chance 0.0482
   eight            5.1733 on  8: 0.647 a degree; chance 0.2611
   nine kinds       2.8110 on  8: 0.351 a degree; chance 0.0543
   27 kinds        15.3224 on 26: 0.589 a degree; chance 0.0489
   back-crosses     3.6730 on 15: 0.245 a degree; chance 0.0014
   twenty plants   12.4870 on 20: 0.624 a degree; chance 0.1017
   the 42 separate tests: smallest chance of a worse fit 0.155 (plant 5, colour of albumen), then 0.157 (true-breeding: colour of pod (100)), 0.178 (plant 8, colour of albumen); if honest, all 42 would stay above 0.155 with chance 0.0009
B. Optional stopping's own fingerprint: the share of the 35 inside the band (|z| at or below 0.5)
   observed 11 of 35; honest expectation 13.4; under optional stopping 28.4 on average, and 11 or fewer in 0.0% of 1000 simulated tables; largest |z| under stopping: median 2.24
C. Do the two models fitted to the 35 simple tests account for the whole table of 84 degrees of freedom?
   cut-off (a test is done again whenever its chance of a worse fit is below 0.155, the cut fitted on the 35): expected total 59.4; a total at or below the observed 41.61 in 0.68% of 200000 tables
      two characters, nine kinds           observed  2.811 on  8; honest 8; cut-off  6.72; shrunk  4.53
      three characters, 27 kinds           observed 15.322 on 26; honest 26; cut-off 23.81; shrunk 14.71
