      back-cross 3                         observed  0.862 on  3; honest 3; cut-off  2.18; shrunk  1.70
      back-cross 2                         observed  0.618 on  3; honest 3; cut-off  2.17; shrunk  1.70
      back-cross 4                         observed  0.531 on  3; honest 3; cut-off  2.19; shrunk  1.70
      back-cross, flower colour and stem   observed  1.084 on  3; honest 3; cut-off  2.18; shrunk  1.70
   shrunk (every deviation reduced to 0.752 of itself): expected total 47.5; a total at or below the observed with chance 0.215
   the 35 alone: observed 19.80; cut-off expects 17.93; shrunk 19.80 (fitted to it)
   the other 49 degrees (seven multi-class tests): observed 21.81, that is 0.445 a degree; chance if honest 0.00027
D. The 35 in two halves: fifteen experiments, twenty single plants
   fifteen experiments  mean z squared 0.487; largest |z| 1.414 (honest chance of none larger 0.077); cut-off over shrunk 2.8; as large or larger under the shrunk model in 44.9% of sets
   twenty plants        mean z squared 0.624; largest |z| 1.424 (honest chance of none larger 0.035); cut-off over shrunk 11.1; as large or larger under the shrunk model in 8.5% of sets
E. The six tests of 100 plants against Fisher's corrected expectation in place of Mendel's 2 to 1
   z: +0.23 +1.67 -0.60 +0.85 +1.88 +0.43; sum of squares 7.66 on 6 (against 2 to 1: 4.57)
F. How many peas is the shrinking? Experiment 1 (7,324 seeds)
   one standard deviation is 37.1 seeds; an honest count misses by 29.6 on average; shrinking every miss by 25% would move 7.3 seeds, 0.10% of them
G. The cut-off as a rule about first attempts
   share of honest first attempts beyond 1.424 standard deviations: 0.155; among 15 experiments that is 2.3 done again on average, among 35 tests 5.4
H. The extremes Mendel reports among his plants (43 round to 2 angular; 14 to 15; 32 yellow to 1 green; 20 to 19)
   43:2  z = +3.18; among 253 honest plants at least one so extreme with chance about 0.31 (normal approximation)
   14:15  z = -3.32; among 253 honest plants at least one so extreme with chance about 0.20 (normal approximation)
   32:1  z = +2.91; among 258 honest plants at least one so extreme with chance about 0.60 (normal approximation)
   20:19  z = -3.42; among 258 honest plants at least one so extreme with chance about 0.15 (normal approximation)
